  "facts": [
    "Handler original hook calls, return values, compaction and event order are preserved.",
    "Each actual Add installation allocates a new ID after OnOverwrite and before OnShielded; map is object to latest installed instance, not once-per-pointer.",
    "Diona skill.go re-adds the same *Tmpl, so its old/new installation receipts remain separate.",
    "All audited Shield implementations derive ShieldOwner from *Tmpl and actual constructors/Add sites pass *Tmpl or pointers to custom shield structs; no address exposed.",
    "Birth HP source and mutable last HP source are separate.",
    "Only explicit birth site allows ability producer/invocation ownership; active hit callback takes precedence and remains separately identified.",
    "Shield hooks capture exact tagged queued attack census; generic ability producer and invocation census excludes those references.",
    "Phase snapshot remains unchanged; monotonic observational shield identity is confined to separate shieldInstances and shieldHooks receipts."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only audited character queue sites emit attributed damage; lifecycle observation does not establish full skill scope.",
    "Shield dot task chains and delayed shield child tasks need separate explicit producer bindings.",
    "Generic lifecycle receipts do not resolve custom implementation private-state phase coverage gaps."
  ],
